description:
Italian, 18th / 19th century
Group of 5 Cameos

Agate and shell, mounted on a later green marble plaque within an ebonised and green marble frame with gilt copper alloy mounts

Incorporating (left to right by row from the top):

An Italian 18th-century agate cameo with a cupid riding a lion;

An Italian first half 19th-century agate cameo with Apollo driving a quadriga;

An Italian early 19th-century shell cameo with a youth;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with cupid enchained;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with cupid holding a butterfly

frame: 28 by 23cm., 11 by 9in.

Importation of these lots into the U.S. may be prohibited or may require licenses and certificates issued by the appropriate agencies (U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service) to be exported and additional licenses and certificates to be imported. U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service reserves the right to block export into the US. Fish and Wild Life reserves the right to block export to the U.S. The inability of a buyer to export or import these lots, or a confiscation by a government agency, cannot justify a delay in payment or the cancellation of a sale.

