description:
French or German, 15th century
A group of six various metal mounted 'cuir bouilli' covered caskets

comprising:

a tooled 'cuir bouilli' casket with domed lid, folding handle, wrought-iron hasp lock with key, hinges and mounts, the tooled leather incorporating Gothic script, the interior lined with red leather, 15.3 by 21.9 by 13.7cm., 6 by 8⅝ by 5⅜ in.;

one similar tooled 'cuir bouilli' casket, with angular hinged lid, wrought iron folding handle, hasp lock, hinges and mounts, the interior lined with paper, 11 by 19.5 by 11.5cm., 4⅜ by 7⅝ by 4½ in.;

a small polychrome and gilt leather casket, with domed hinged lid, folding handle and hasp lock, brass hinges and mounts, the interior lined with red velvet, 10 by 17 by 10cm., 4 by 6¾ by 4in.;

a small tooled 'cuir bouilli' and brass mounted casket, with angular lid, brass folding handle, hasp lock, hinges and mounts, the interior lined with red silk fabric, 7.5 by 15 by 10cm., 3 by 5⅞ by 4in.;

A French tooled 'cuir bouilli' missal box, 15th century, with angular hinged lid, wrought iron folding handles, hasp lock, hinges and mounts, the interior lined with red leather, 8.5 by 19.5 by17cm., 3⅜ by 7⅝ by 6¾ in.

one further similar tooled 'cuir bouilli' casket, with angular hinged lid, wrought iron folding handle, hasp lock, hinges and mounts, with its key, the interior lined with red leather, with inventory number 1969.7 inscribed with black ink, 10.5 by 18.3 by 11.5cm., 4⅛ by 7¼ by 4½ in.

(6)

